# @hub-lanes

# blocked-resolver (operator line, outside managed blocks; the operator 2026-09-13
# "the reality is I will never do a human review"). Every park that used to wait
# on a person — conductor BLOCKED_HUMAN rows, pool rows parked failed, the
# REVIEW_BLOCKED gates, review-rescue's give-ups — is drained here on an agent
# ladder (rebuild fresh / fix round / adjudicate) and, when that is exhausted,
# recorded as ABANDONED with ONE alert listing what was tried. */10 at minute
# 4,14,... so it never shares a tick with the merge conductor (*/5) or the merge
# sweep (6,16,...). Kill: flags/blocked-resolver-disabled; dry run:
# flags/blocked-resolver-observe. docs/MERGE-CONDUCTOR.md section 11.
# C2 (2026-09-24): a BACKSTOP now — bin/lib/cadence-backstop.sh lets a tick
# through every lib.cadence-backstop.cadence_backstop_min_blocked_resolver
# minutes (default 30; 0 = every tick, as before), or at once when the conductor
# has written a new hand-off (state/merge-conductor/handoff). Fail-open: only the
# gate's deliberate rc 3 skips; a missing, broken or aborted gate runs the lane.
# BH-5913 (2026-10-10): --dispatch scans nothing. It starts one detached
# `blocked-resolver.sh <project>` per project, each on its own lock and at a
# stable offset inside BR_DISPATCH_SPREAD_SECS (bin/lib/project-lanes.sh).
4,14,24,34,44,54 * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && { /root/harness/bin/lib/cadence-backstop.sh blocked-resolver --wake-dir /root/harness/state/merge-conductor/handoff; [ $? -ne 3 ]; } && /root/harness/bin/blocked-resolver.sh --dispatch >> /root/harness/logs/blocked-resolver-cron.log 2>&1
